             "baseline_note_2026_08_10": "6.9 → 7.8 re-baselined 2026-08-10. WHICH OF THE TWO THIS IS, stated because the guard asks: a RATCHET RESET, not the config bent around a failing check — and the discriminator is that the payload is real and needed rather than that the check was inconvenient. The 44 KB is two source files a shipped instruction depends on, the cheaper alternative was examined and rejected on that ground (below), the new cap carries ~8% headroom over the higher of two disagreeing measurements rather than clearing by a hair, and the raise was put to the maintainer as a decision instead of applied to make a red go away. A reader who disagrees has everything needed to reverse it: the measurement, its method, the trip cause, and the rejected option. Maintainer-decided in the PR that tripped it, surfaced rather than smuggled — the same standing this file's `owner: maintainer` requires. MEASURED TWICE, and the two do not agree: CI reported 6.907 on this exact commit, a local run under the documented conditions reports 7.238. The 331 KB gap is UNEXPLAINED — the tree matches the pushed commit and only this file differs — so the cap is set over the HIGHER figure rather than the convenient one, and the discrepancy is recorded here as an open question instead of resolved by assumption. A third party reproducing this should expect either number and should not treat the lower one as authoritative. Separately, and this part IS understood: `npm pack --dry-run --ignore-scripts` in a worktree that has been BUILT reads 8.45, because the flag assumes dist/cli, dist/ui, dist/mcp and dist/hooks are absent and a built tree has them. That figure is not comparable to this budget and must never be written here — recorded because it is a trap the documented method invites. Trip cause: road-to-conformance-round5 Phase 3 added src/scripts/hooks/turn_end_gate_hook.ts (32 KB) and src/scripts/measure_turn_end_gate.ts (12 KB) in packed paths plus schema/template/contract growth, landing 7 KB over a 6.9 cap. Max set to 7.8 (~8% headroom over 7.238, and ~13% over CI's 6.907) for the reason the 2026-08-05 note already gives: a cap pinned just above the measurement reds on the next commit and teaches the reader to raise it again. ALTERNATIVE EXAMINED AND REJECTED, so it is not re-proposed: dropping measure_turn_end_gate.ts from the pack would have cleared the cap with room, but the settings description added in the same change instructs CONSUMERS to run that script against their own transcript store before arming the gate — excluding it would break a shipped instruction.",
             "baseline_note": "5.903 → 6.398 re-baselined 2026-08-05. This is a RE-BASELINE, not a carve-out for the change that tripped it: measured on the tracked tree, `origin/main` alone was already at 6.372 of a 6.4 cap, so 28 KB of headroom remained after months of accretion and the next legitimate addition of any size was going to cross it. The addition here is 26 KB — docs/contracts/settings-classes.md (the A/B/C fence, read at RUNTIME by the settings writer, so it must ship) plus src/server/io/yamlIO.ts (imported by that writer to preserve the user's comments). CI measures ~4 KB above the local figure because it regenerates dist/agent-src first. Max set to 6.9 rather than to a number that merely clears: a cap pinned 2 KB above the measurement reds on the next commit and teaches the reader to raise it again, which is how a budget becomes a formality. That restores the ~8% headroom the 5.903/6.4 pair originally carried. The `owner: maintainer` on this file stands — this raise is surfaced in the PR for that decision, not smuggled.",
